image_description:
Morphological diversity of Pilea and Achudemia. 
A, P. longicaulis (shrub); 
B, P. fairchildiana (shrub, with alternate, spirally arranged leaves);
C, A. boniana (herb, epipetric); 
D, P. paniculigera (herb, epipetric); 
E, P. matama (unequal opposite leaves, epiphytic with capitate female inflorescences); 
F, P. peploides (herb, clumped); 
G, P. aff. microphylla; 
H, P. rivularis (female inflorescence enclosed by stipules); 
I, P. aff. pittieri (herb, male capitate inflorescence arising from stolons); 
J, P. angustifolia (herb, male capitate inflorescence); 
K, P. notata (male cyme inflorescence). — 

A, B, E & G–J by Alexandre K. Monro; D by Yi-Gang Wei; C, D, F & K by Long-Fei Fu.
